## consolidate retro
- Ingested 128 contributions (123 enrich, 5 travel references): 0 quarantined, 0 lint
  failures, 0 GE-sourcing hits, 1 late-duplicate dropped (none existed). All refs
  manifest-validated (slug present + title char-exact).
- Merged: 86 steps.jsonl rows gained refs/atom/hints/mapMarkers; 37-entry step_refs.jsonl
  sidecar minted for non-row emitted ids (milestone/steer/synth/chkpt/planner-bg); 93 rows
  no scrambler covered got derived refs (17 new pages fetched: 6 training guides, NMZ,
  Maniacal monkey, 5 quests, 5 RFD subpages). steps-with-refs: 123/123 route-p2p,
  186/186 route-corpus; 0 refs point outside manifest.jsonl. npm test 73/73, no re-pin
  (step sets/labels unchanged — enrichment is additive).
- enrich.py: registry-stable chkpt ids (was per-route emission order), row mapMarkers
  override catalog zone pins, universal by-id refs/markers fill pass (covers milestone/
  steer/bg/checkpoint emitters that drop refs).
- §C.5 PROPOSED-ID→new-rows deferred to Lane 5 as 78 lane5:* queue tickets (+1 xref-index):
  proposals carry contributor-flagged ASSUMED prereqs, and minting rows renumbers synth-*
  ids which would orphan this very pass's synth-keyed refs. Same for consolidate-xp fixes.
- CANONICAL-TRIGGER MINT: when a briefing hands parallel agents generated ids
  (chkpt-*/synth-*), it must state the id-generation rule and require quoting the
  human-readable anchor (checkpoint label) beside the id — two domains numbered the same
  checkpoints by different conventions and only the quoted labels made consolidation
  unambiguous.

## extrapolate retro
- Read all four ledgers + chain + both design docs; wrote study/EXTRAPOLATION.md:
  145 equal-grade checklist items (36 GAP insertions), 12 named gaps (G1-G12),
  8 wave3:* scope bundles queued with self-contained JSON briefs.
- Compounding held: every scope's "have" list names already-fetched manifest slugs
  (10+ blobs fetched at consolidation were never mined — wave 3 mines before fetching);
  net-new fetch surface across all 8 scopes is ~30 pages, versus ~36 gaps.
- Equal-grade rule honored: scaffolded finer items (pps-*, ctr-*) sit at the same rank
  as quests/milestones; grouping is PHASE/CHKPT labels only, per GRANULARITY §7.
- G12 (data-fix backlog) deliberately got NO wave-3 scope: it is already grounded and
  ticketed (78 lane5:* + coord-fix + consolidate-xp) — re-scoping it would duplicate
  the ledger, the exact failure the compound rule exists to prevent.
- CANONICAL-TRIGGER MINT: a directive that asks for "gaps vs the checklist" must state
  whether already-ticketed known fixes count as gaps — this pass classed them as a gap
  ROW (G12) but excluded them from wave scoping, and only the ledger cross-check made
  that call defensible. Future extrapolation briefs should say: "gap = missing knowledge
  or missing rows; open tickets are inventory, not gaps — list them once, scope them never."
